    <GaugingStation location="Broughton" name="Broughton Brook" number="33031">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Station modified in 1977 gauging a flat catchment with greedsand bedrock, significant artificial influences due to public water supply abstraction.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Flume was subject to drowning but flows were corrected. Current rating includes floodplain flow and accounts for drowning. One peak flow rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Flat V Crump profile weir 7.0m wide installed in 1977 when river realigned. Prior to 23/6/77 trapezoidal critical depth flume 7.4m wide, horizontal crest 1m wide, located at SP892405.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2023 (WINFAP Files v12).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Runoff influenced by groundwater abstraction and recharge. One Greensand groundwater puclic water supply abstraction accounts for virtually all the abstraction in the catchment. Station located near Cotton Valley STW. Runoff increased by effluent return.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly flat, the edge just impinging on the Chiltern escarpment. Clay and Greensand catchment, with some Boulder Clay cover. Mixed agricultural land use with some forestry in S, and significant urban development.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">GE</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Although not gauged to within 30% of QMED, all flows contained and theoretical rating expected to perform well." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="All flows contained and theoretical rating expected to perform well." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
